<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Simone Martini</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1284–<a href="/years/1344">1344</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Simone Martini was a Sienese painter, a follower of Duccio and one of the most influential artists of the 14th century. His works include the Maestà fresco of 1315 in Siena's Palazzo Pubblico and the Annunciation of 1333, now in the Uffizi. He worked for the Angevin court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> and at the papal court in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avignon">Avignon</a>, where he knew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrarch">Petrarch</a> and died in 1344.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/simone-martini.jpg" alt="Simone Martini" width="320" height="453" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Simone Martini · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Simone_Martini_-_Frontispice_du_Virgile.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
